Z||000013||rogergarrison||06-11-2000||10:30 PM||||I put my own turbo kit in winter before last. Fairly simple job. just be careful about how much boost u adjust in. Iv run up to 12lbs experimenting with the wastegate, but settled in on around 4 1/2 lbs. Lots better for engine life. ive put over 30k on it with very minor problems, not turbo related. I have a boost gage mounted in dash to monitor and being in a Ferrari kit, the louvers behind the drivers window was ideal place to run intercooler. Im working on a possible water injection for even more power. For those who arent familiar, some WWII fighter aircraft used water injection (a mist of water sprayed into the intake to cool the air/fuel mixture, making it much more dense) to give quick boosts in performance similar to nitros but not as potent. And waters cheap. Go for the turbo, I love it.<P>RG||||reg||1
